# smallFish configuration template.
#
# ./setup.sh copies this to app.env and points the two path settings at your
# checkout. It never overwrites an existing app.env.
#
# app.env is git-ignored and becomes a credential store the moment you fill it
# in. Keep it private; never commit it or paste it into an issue.
#
# EVERY credential below is optional. The core application — stocks, ETFs,
# portfolios, sectors, momentum, wheel screening, and the bundled Research
# Studies — works with all of them blank. See docs/CONFIGURATION.md for what
# each setting unlocks, and docs/BROKERAGES.md for guided setup.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- required

# Runtime locations. ./setup.sh fills these in with this checkout's data/ and
# logs/ directories. Absolute paths; point them elsewhere to keep generated
# data outside the repository.
SFP_DATA_DIR=/absolute/path/to/smallFish/data
SFP_LOG_DIR=/absolute/path/to/smallFish/logs

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- FastAPI

# The service has no authentication layer. Keep it bound to localhost and do
# not expose it directly to the internet. See docs/SUPPORT_MATRIX.md.
APP_HOST=127.0.0.1
APP_PORT=8000
CORS_ORIGINS=http://localhost:4200

# ------------------------------------------------------- optional: earnings

# Finnhub earnings calendar. Without it, the upcoming-earnings feed and the
# live pre-earnings scan are unavailable; everything else works.
# Free key: https://finnhub.io/register
FINNHUB_API_KEY=

# ----------------------------------------------------- optional: Tastytrade

# Read-only options-activity import and DXLink quotes/Greeks/beta.
# Guided setup: ./setup-brokerages.sh setup tastytrade
# Leave TT_ENV at sandbox unless you intend to read your live account.
TT_CLIENT_SECRET=
TT_REFRESH_TOKEN=
TT_ENV=sandbox

# Optional comma-separated symbols kept outside the broker activity ledger.
SFP_OPTIONS_ACTIVITY_EXCLUDED_SYMBOLS=

# ------------------------------------------------------ optional: SnapTrade

# Read-only holdings import for a retirement brokerage such as Fidelity.
# Fidelity connects THROUGH SnapTrade; smallFish never receives Fidelity
# credentials. Guided setup: ./setup-brokerages.sh setup snaptrade
SNAPTRADE_CLIENT_ID=
SNAPTRADE_CONSUMER_KEY=
# Personal keys (PERS- client-id prefix) are single-user: link brokerages on
# the SnapTrade dashboard and leave the two settings below empty. Commercial
# keys must first register a user — ./setup-brokerages.sh setup snaptrade
# walks through it — and save the returned credentials here.
SNAPTRADE_USER_ID=
SNAPTRADE_USER_SECRET=

# ------------------------------------------------- optional: path overrides

# Advanced. Each defaults to a path under SFP_DATA_DIR; set one only to move a
# specific artifact. See docs/CONFIGURATION.md.
# SFP_SNAPTRADE_HOLDINGS=/absolute/path/to/data/ledger_retirement/snaptrade_holdings.csv
# SFP_OPTIONS_GREEKS=/absolute/path/to/data/ledger_options/options_greeks.csv
# SFP_OPTIONS_BETAS=/absolute/path/to/data/ledger_options/options_betas.csv
# SFP_STUDIES_DIR=/absolute/path/to/data/studies
